  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Abdul Khaddar vs The State Of Kerala on 6 September, 2012 Author: P.Bhavadasan Bench: P.Bhavadasan In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr.Justice P.Bhavadasan Thursday, The 6Th Day Of September 2012/15Th Bhadra 1934 Bail Appl..No. 5963 of 2012 () ------------------------------ (Crime No.732/2012 Of Museum Police Station, Thiruvananthapuram District) Petitioners/Accused: ------------------- 1. Abdul Khaddar, Aged 50 Years S/O.Muhammad, Flat No.3A, Heaven Pundit'S Colony, Kuravankonam Ward, Kowdiar Thiruvananthapuram From Kalannoor Veedu Kalannoorpuram Desom, Bayar Village Kasaragod Taluk (A1) 2. Jaleel, Aged 27 Years S/O.Muhammed, H.No.A72, Sasthamangalam Sasthamangalam Village From B.C.House, Kukar Desom Mangalpad, Uppalam Village, Kasaragod (A2) 3. Rajkumar Sahu, Aged 22 Years S/O.Munnan Sahu, Santhoshpur Desom, Mirgon Village Vidanappur District, Bangal (A3) 4. Jenthu Sett, Aged 20 Years S/P.Panchanian Sett, Mijigeru Desom, Pulamon Village Poorva Midhinapur, West Bengal (A4) By Adv. Sri.Sasthamangalam S. Ajithkumar Abdul Khaddar vs The State Of Kerala on 6 September, 2012 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/91794200/ 1 Respondent/Complainant: ---------------------- The State Of Kerala Represented By Public Prosecutor High Court Of Kerala, Ernakulam. By Public Prosecutor Smt. Kochumol Koduvall.",
    "facts": "This is an application for bail under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure filed by accused Nos.1 to 4 in Crime No.732 of 2012 of Museum Police Station, Thiruvananthapuram for having committed offences under Sections 328, 304 and 34 IPC read with 59(III) of the Food Safety & Standards Act 2006. 2. The prosecution allegation appears is that the first petitioner is the proprietor of a hotel by name \"Salwa Cafe\" and the others are employees who cooks putrefied chicken and served to continue causing ill health to some persons and also causing death of one person. The petitioners are in custody from 18.7.2012 onwards.",
    "arguments": "3. The learned counsel for the petitioners points out that petitioners are innocent and have been falsely implicated with ulterior motive. At any rate, it is pointed out that since the investigation has progressed to a good extent, their continued custody is unnecessary. They expressed their willings to abide by any conditions if bail is granted. 4. The learned Public Prosecutor very vehemently opposed the petition. As far as the first petitioner is concerned, it is pointed out that he was involved in similar incident for the year 2007 and pointed out that the investigation is yet to be completed and therefore, petitioners may not be granted bail. 5. The allegation is that 1st petitioner and others cookes putrefied chicken and served to several customers causing ill health to some persons and also causing death of one person.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. The learned counsel for the petitioners points out that petitioners are innocent and have been falsely implicated with ulterior motive. At any rate, it is pointed out that since the investigation has progressed to a good extent, their continued custody is unnecessary.",
    "respondent_arguments": "They expressed their willings to abide by any conditions if bail is granted. 4. The learned Public Prosecutor very vehemently opposed the petition. As far as the first petitioner is concerned, it is pointed out that he was involved in similar incident for the year 2007 and pointed out that the investigation is yet to be completed and therefore, petitioners may not be granted bail. 5. The allegation is that 1st petitioner and others cookes putrefied chicken and served to several customers causing ill health to some persons and also causing death of one person.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
